WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.790
If you want to hear my theory about how Ellie
Creed from Pet Sematary, as well as two other

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.800
characters in that story have the same ability
as Danny Torrence from The Shining, then stick

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.780
around to the end of this video.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.760
Stephen King’s third full-length novel,
The Shining, is titled after an ability held

00:00:17.769 --> 00:00:18.990
by a few of the characters.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.490
The man to introduce us to the ability says
that he and his grandmother call it “the

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.490
shine”.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.210
It can be described as a psychic and clairvoyant
power, whose intensity varies from individual

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.210
to individual.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.720
Dick Halloran is the name of the head chef
at The Overlook Hotel who teaches Danny everything

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.090
he knows about the shine.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.610
He explains that he and his Grandmother used
to have entire conversations without ever

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.600
opening their mouths.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.920
“She called it shining.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.080
And for a long time I thought it was just
the two of us that had the shine to us.”

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.500
But, it’s not.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.350
Halloran explains that there aren’t a lot
of people who shine, but he has run across

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.140
maybe 50 or 60 who have a little bit of shine
to them.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:57.421
So what does shining actually consist of,
and why do I think that Ellie, from Pet Sematary

00:00:57.421 --> 00:00:58.720
has the shine?

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:02.010
As Dick mentioned, those who shine are capable
of telepathic communication.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:05.649
Danny is also able to hear the thoughts of
those who don’t shine, like how he hears

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:07.759
Mrs. Brant’s thoughts about the hotel’s
valet, Mike.

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:13.570
Now I’m not going to say what those thoughts
consisted of… but….

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.020
When Halloran asks Danny if he listens to
his parents’ thoughts, he says he tries

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.009
not to invade their privacy, but he can’t
help picking up on their feelings or emotions.

00:01:21.009 --> 00:01:24.979
There is evidence of Ellie reading her father’s
mind, or at the very least picking up on his

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:26.560
feelings in Pet Sematary.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.209
The family goes to visit Ellie’s Grandma
and Grandpa on her mother’s side, but Louis

00:01:30.209 --> 00:01:31.209
doesn’t go with.

00:01:31.209 --> 00:01:35.200
Louis strongly dislikes his father-in-law
because he tried to bribe Louis out of marrying

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.859
Rachel, making him quite possibly the champion
of stereotypical in-law characters in fiction.

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:43.310
Ellie somehow seems to know the real reason,
and asks her father if he he’s pissed off

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.810
at Grandpa, to which Louis wonders how she
possibly could have known that.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:50.740
Halloran also warns Danny about some bad dreams
that he’s had at the Overlook.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:54.369
He tells him, “People who shine can sometimes
see things that are gonna happen, and I think

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:56.780
sometimes they can see things that did happen.”

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.229
When Ellie is away at her grandparents’
house, she has a dream of her cat, Church,

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:04.100
dying the night that Church is run over by
a truck and buried in the Mic Mac burial ground.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.280
"I dreamed he got hit by a car and you and
Mr Crandall buried him in the Pet Sematary.”

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.960
“That was a silly dream, wasn’t it?”

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.530
But it wasn’t too silly of a dream, and
Ellie continues to have dreams about past

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.850
and future events.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.970
But if you don’t want to get the ending
of Pet Sematary spoiled for you, I would not

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.780
watch any more of this video, why don’t
you check this one out instead?

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:28.330
Those of you who have read the book may remember,
that Ellie’s next dream involves Louis being

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.040
dead, a prediction of the end of Pet Sematary.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.490
And when Ellie and Rachel are about to leave
on the plane, Ellie begs her father to let

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.620
them stay, or for him to come with, and I
think this is because she senses her father’s

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.860
life will be in danger.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.800
She also expresses more of her fears to Louis
at the airport.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.100
“Daddy, I dreamed we were at Gage’s funeral
and the funeral man opened his coffin and

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.100
it was empty.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.650
Then I dreamed I was home and I looked at
Gage’s crib and that was empty too.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.060
But there was dirt in it.”

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:57.340
This is just before Louis goes to dig up Gage
and try to revive him in the Mic Mac burial

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.340
ground.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:02.060
The first dream represents the fact that Louis
will empty Gage’s coffin in Pleasantview

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:05.510
Cemetery; and the second one is a reminder
of when the ghost of Victor Pascow tried to

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.620
warn Louis in the night not to go on to the
cursed burial ground, and Louis wakes up with

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.430
the dirt of the Pet Sematary path on his feet
in bed the next morning.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:16.650
Just before boarding the plane, Ellie begs
one last time.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.910
Listen to this portion.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.380
Ellie gazed at him solemnly with her sybil’s
eyes.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:24.400
“I don’t want to go,” she said again,
but so low that only Louis could really hear

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.700
over the shuffle and murmur of the boarding
passengers.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.030
“I don’t want Mommy to go either.”

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:30.950
“Ellie, come on,” Louis said.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:31.950
“You’ll be fine.”

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.480
“I’ll be fine,’ she said, ‘but what
about you?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.660
Daddy, what about you?”

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:40.070
I find it very interesting that King uses
describes Ellie’s gaze as having come through

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:43.910
sybil’s eyes, a word derived from the Greek
word “sibulla” which described a woman

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.710
who utters the oracles and prophecies of a
god.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:50.420
Shortly after, Ellie has another vision on
the plane, where she describes Gage coming

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.580
alive again and weilding a knife.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.250
What happens next is interesting if you think
about another aspect of the shine that Dick

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.970
Halloran describes to Danny.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.600
He asks Danny to contact him if there is any
trouble at the Overlook, that he might even

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.840
hear his call way down in Florida.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.267
Danny later does use this to call for help
when all other lines of communication have

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:09.110
been cut, sending Halloran on his way to try
to rescue the Torrance family.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:12.201
Personally, I probably would have the just
let the little **** die, I mean it’s so

00:04:12.201 --> 00:04:15.870
much colder in Colorado than it is in Florida,
why would you leave?

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:19.370
Something similar happens in Pet Sematary,
however, instead of the child calling out

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.710
for help, it is the ghost of Victor Pascow
who contacts Ellie in her dream and takes

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:27.820
her to the Pet Sematary in an attempt to try
to get her to tell Rachel what she had seen.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:31.690
It’s possible that this isn’t an example
of a “long distance call” using the Shining

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:35.540
though, because maybe Pascow is just able
to travel anywhere because he’s a ghost.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.880
This does send Rachel on her way to try to
put a stop to Louis’s actions.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.590
However, it seems unlikely that she would
randomly take the word of a 6 year old based

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.210
on a bad dream she had.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:48.060
This is why I think that Rachel has a little
bit of a shine to her as well; in fact, when

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.940
Halloran did mention that he thinks all mothers
shine a little, at least until their kids

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:53.730
grow up enough to watch out for themselves.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:57.620
This would also explain why Pascow is able
help Rachel throughout the latter part of

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:58.620
the story.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.810
But there’s one more character that I think
has a tiny bit of shine as well.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:05.300
When Rachel is on her way back from Chicago,
she phones Jud Crandall to see if he knows

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.740
why Louis isn’t home.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.410
When speaking to her, he mentions that she
sounds closer, and although she did sound

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.180
closer somehow, he hears the sound of the
wind on the line, and it reminds him of the

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.500
sound of dead voices sighing in chorus.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:21.140
I don’t think Jud or Rachel realize they
have the shine, but if he does have some faint

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:25.020
sign of it, it would explain how he senses
that Louis was getting ideas about burying

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.480
Gage in the Mic Mac grounds.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.480
“You’re thinking of puttin’ him up there.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.360
Don’t deny the thought hadn’t crossed
your mind Louis.”

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.930
There is one more major aspect of the shine
though, that leads me to believe that Ellie

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:38.830
has pretty strong case of it.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.460
When Halloran is trying to gauge how strong
Danny’s shine is, he asks him to blast a

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:43.840
thought as hard as he can.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.560
Danny is much more powerful than anticipated
though.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:50.430
Halloran flies back in his seat and his injured
by the force of Danny’s shine, which he

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.680
compares to a Nolan Ryan fastball.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.960
Ellie may be channeling a little Fergie Jenkins
herself, because after Rachel leaves to go

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.520
back to Ludlow, her father phones Louis about
a dream Ellie had, that is so powerful they

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.590
end up taking her to the hospital.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.010
Let me know in the comments if you can come
up with any other Stephen King characters

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:09.740
who have the shine, and watch this video if
you want to hear some of the things you might

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.610
have missed in Stephen King’s IT.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:16.310
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.400
notifications, and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.669
Assuming we both survive.

